Create a modular router-adapter system. Do not build one generic connector that assumes every manufacturer has the same API.

Every router record must include:

- Tenant/owner ID.
- Router name and site.
- Manufacturer and model.
- Router firmware or controller version where available.
- Connection method.
- Management endpoint or controller ID.
- Secure credential reference.
- Supported capabilities.
- Last successful connection time.
- Last health-check result.
- Current status and error details.
- Configuration and authorization status.
- Script or connector enrollment status.
- Last script generation time.
- Last successful enrollment time.
- Active enrollment token status.

Build a common adapter interface with operations such as:

- Test connection.
- Read router information.
- Read health and uptime.
- List supported client sessions.
- Authorize a paid customer.
- Disconnect a customer.
- Create or revoke a voucher where supported.
- Read traffic and bandwidth statistics where supported.
